        "description": "Track 05 from \"Bowery Poetry Club, August '03\", TILT Brass' second Non-Site Records \"SoundCloud Releases (SCR)\" series release. Elliott Sharp's 1998 \"SyndaKit\", written for his Orchestra Carbon project, is a tour de force of open form composition meant to groove incessantly hard. From the program note:\r\n\r\n\"The essence of SyndaKit is a transformative groove composed of 144 'Cores' divided among the... players and manifested through processes of imitation, addition, recombination, transposition, and improvisation.\" \r\n\r\nThis was TILT's first of 3 performances of the piece. We had only just begun to learn the process which would be obvious to initiated E# listeners. Regardless, a great deal of fascinating improvisative activity rises forth as only this group of TILT family members could manifest. \r\n\r\nPersonnel:\r\nDave Ballou, Russ Johnson, Jon Nelson - trumpet \r\nGreg Evans, Tom Varner – French horn \r\nCurtis Hasselbring, Christopher McIntyre – trombone \r\nJulie Kalu – bass trombone  \r\nDave Hofstra – tuba  \r\nKevin Norton – percussion",
